      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Today's date is: {{ $now.format('yyyy-MM-dd') }}\nuser message: {{$json.messages[0].text.body }}\nYour task:\nAnalyze the user message and return ONLY valid JSON.\n\nExtract these fields:\n* user_message\n* isExpense\n* amount\n* location\n* category\n* date\n\nRules:\n\n1. If the user is REPORTING an expense\n   Examples:\n\n* \"I spent 200 at KFC\"\n* \"Paid 500 for lunch\"\n* \"Uber cost me 300\"\n\nThen:\n\n* set \"isExpense\" to true\n* extract all possible fields\n\n2. If the user is ASKING about expenses\n   Examples:\n* \"How much did I spend on lunch?\"\n* \"Show my food expenses\"\n* \"What was my last expense?\"\n\nThen:\n\n* set \"isExpense\" to false\n* amount = null\n* location = null\n* category = null\n* date = null\n\n3. If no date is mentioned in an expense entry:\n\n* use today's date\n\n4. If some fields are missing:\n\n* use null\n\n5. Return ONLY raw JSON\n\n* no markdown\n* no explanations\n* no extra text\n\n\nExample 1 input:\nI spent 200 at KFC today\n\nExample 1 output:\n{\n\"user_message\": \"I spent 200 at KFC today\",\n\"isExpense\": true,\n\"amount\": 200,\n\"location\": \"KFC\",\n\"category\": \"Food\",\n\"date\": \"{{ $now.format('yyyy-MM-dd') }}\"\n}\n\nExample 2 input:\nHow much did I spend on lunch?\n\nExample 2 output:\n{\n\"user_message\": \"How much did I spend on lunch?\",\n\"isExpense\": false,\n\"amount\": null,\n\"location\": null,\n\"category\": null,\n\"date\": null\n}\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an expense tracking assistant. When users tell you about an expense (e.g., \"I spent $50 at Starbucks\"), extract the usermessage ,amount, location, category, and date. Set isExpense to true. If the user is asking a question about their expenses (e.g., \"how much did I spend this week?\"), set isExpense to false and leave other fields empty. Always use today's date if not specified."
        }
      },
